This system ships with dserv, so it is not local work to push.

config/essconf.tcl's boot ladder falls back to it when a rig has nothing
synced yet, which means it is present in the installed systems tree on every
box. On a rig whose ESS_SYSTEM_PATH IS that tree it would otherwise look
like something written here and never pushed: the Sync badge lights, and a
push would put a copy of the bootstrap in the registry for every rig to pull
back.

lib/ess_scripts-1.0.tm reads this file's existence, not its contents, in
scripts::_excluded -- so if this rig has deliberately forked blinky and
wants its version in the registry, delete this file.
